<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<policyDefinitionResources xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" revision="1.0" schemaVersion="1.0" xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/GroupPolicy/2006/07/PolicyDefinitions">
  <displayName>KSIP settings</displayName>
  <description>Per-user KSIP policies (HKCU\Software\Policies\KashiharaCity\ksip). The audio devices, the network adapter, the extension, and the authentication ID and password differ by machine or user and are not included; nor are the gains and the echo delay, which the user adjusts where the phone is used.</description>
  <resources>
    <stringTable>
      <string id="SUPPORTED_KSIP">KSIP (the versions that keep each setting in a registry value of its own)</string>
      <string id="Category_KashiharaCity">Kashihara City</string>
      <string id="Category_KSIP">KSIP</string>
      <string id="Category_Connection">Account and connection</string>
      <string id="Category_Audio">Audio</string>
      <string id="Category_Calls">Calls and display</string>
      <string id="Category_Links">Links</string>
      <string id="Category_Buttons">Buttons</string>
      <string id="Category_Other">Other</string>
      <string id="ButtonKind_0">Unused (no button)</string>
      <string id="ButtonKind_1">Transfer</string>
      <string id="ButtonKind_2">Dial (with BLF)</string>
      <string id="ButtonKind_3">Dial (no BLF)</string>
      <string id="ButtonKind_4">Park (with BLF)</string>
      <string id="ButtonKind_5">Open a link</string>
      <string id="ButtonKind_6">Do not disturb</string>
      <string id="ButtonKind_7">Voicemail</string>
      <string id="server">SIP server</string>
      <string id="server_Help">Host name or IP address of the SIP server: letters, digits, &quot;.&quot; and &quot;-&quot;, up to 253 characters. Disabled deletes the value and, as not configured, returns to the user's own. (default: 127.0.0.1)

A setting a policy decides cannot be changed in the KSIP settings dialog or the button editing, and is shown as set by the administrator. Not configured returns to what the user saved.

The value is written to the value of the same name under HKCU\Software\Policies\KashiharaCity\ksip. KSIP reads it when it starts, so a change takes effect when KSIP starts again.</string>
      <string id="port">SIP server port</string>
      <string id="port_Help">Port of the SIP server, 1 to 65535. Disabled deletes the value and, as not configured, returns to the user's own. (default: 5060)

A setting a policy decides cannot be changed in the KSIP settings dialog or the button editing, and is shown as set by the administrator. Not configured returns to what the user saved.

The value is written to the value of the same name under HKCU\Software\Policies\KashiharaCity\ksip. KSIP reads it when it starts, so a change takes effect when KSIP starts again.</string>
      <string id="transport">SIP transport</string>
      <string id="transport_Help">Whether SIP signalling goes over UDP, TCP or TLS. Over TLS the server is verified against the chosen certificate authority, or against the Windows Trusted Root Certification Authorities when none is chosen. Disabled deletes the value and, as not configured, returns to the user's own. (default: UDP)

A setting a policy decides cannot be changed in the KSIP settings dialog or the button editing, and is shown as set by the administrator. Not configured returns to what the user saved.

The value is written to the value of the same name under HKCU\Software\Policies\KashiharaCity\ksip. KSIP reads it when it starts, so a change takes effect when KSIP starts again.</string>
      <string id="transport_0">UDP (not encrypted)</string>
      <string id="transport_1">TCP (not encrypted)</string>
      <string id="transport_2">TLS (RFC 3261)</string>
      <string id="media_encryption">Media encryption</string>
      <string id="media_encryption_Help">How call audio is encrypted. SDES and OSRTP carry their keys in the signalling, so KSIP does not connect with them unless the SIP transport is TLS. SDES does not talk to a peer that cannot encrypt; OSRTP falls back to plain audio when the peer returns no key. Disabled deletes the value and, as not configured, returns to the user's own. (default: none)

A setting a policy decides cannot be changed in the KSIP settings dialog or the button editing, and is shown as set by the administrator. Not configured returns to what the user saved.

The value is written to the value of the same name under HKCU\Software\Policies\KashiharaCity\ksip. KSIP reads it when it starts, so a change takes effect when KSIP starts again.</string>
      <string id="media_encryption_0">None</string>
      <string id="media_encryption_1">SRTP required (SDES, RFC 4568)</string>
      <string id="media_encryption_2">Try SRTP (OSRTP, RFC 8643)</string>
      <string id="media_encryption_3">SRTP (DTLS-SRTP, RFC 5764)</string>
      <string id="ca_file">Trusted certificate authority</string>
      <string id="ca_file_Help">Path of the certificate authority (PEM) that TLS verifies the server against, up to 400 characters. Disabled deletes the value and, as not configured, returns to the user's own. (default: the Windows certificate store)

A setting a policy decides cannot be changed in the KSIP settings dialog or the button editing, and is shown as set by the administrator. Not configured returns to what the user saved.

The value is written to the value of the same name under HKCU\Software\Policies\KashiharaCity\ksip. KSIP reads it when it starts, so a change takes effect when KSIP starts again.</string>
      <string id="codecs">Audio codecs and their order</string>
      <string id="codecs_Help">The audio codecs to offer, in order, separated by commas: from opus, G722, PCMU and PCMA; one not listed is not used. KSIP does not connect with a name repeated or unknown. Example: PCMU,opus. Disabled deletes the value and, as not configured, returns to the user's own. (default: opus,G722,PCMU,PCMA)

A setting a policy decides cannot be changed in the KSIP settings dialog or the button editing, and is shown as set by the administrator. Not configured returns to what the user saved.

The value is written to the value of the same name under HKCU\Software\Policies\KashiharaCity\ksip. KSIP reads it when it starts, so a change takes effect when KSIP starts again.</string>
      <string id="dtmf_mode">DTMF method</string>
      <string id="dtmf_mode_Help">How key presses (DTMF) are sent. RTP (RFC 4733) is the usual way; choose SIP INFO or in-band when the PBX asks for it. In-band is sent as sound, so G.711 is the codec it works with most surely. In band, each digit is a 100 ms tone and a 100 ms pause, which meets the timing of Japan’s MIC Notice No. 357 of 2024, Appended Table 2 (push-button dial signals: tone 50 ms or more, pause 30 ms or more, period 120 ms or more). Disabled deletes the value and, as not configured, returns to the user's own. (default: RTP)

A setting a policy decides cannot be changed in the KSIP settings dialog or the button editing, and is shown as set by the administrator. Not configured returns to what the user saved.

The value is written to the value of the same name under HKCU\Software\Policies\KashiharaCity\ksip. KSIP reads it when it starts, so a change takes effect when KSIP starts again.</string>
      <string id="dtmf_mode_0">RTP (RFC 4733)</string>
      <string id="dtmf_mode_1">SIP INFO</string>
      <string id="dtmf_mode_2">In band (as sound)</string>
      <string id="sip_port">Local SIP port</string>
      <string id="sip_port_Help">The port KSIP listens for SIP on, 1024 to 65535. KSIP does not connect when it falls within the RTP ports. Disabled deletes the value and, as not configured, returns to the user's own. (default: 5060)

A setting a policy decides cannot be changed in the KSIP settings dialog or the button editing, and is shown as set by the administrator. Not configured returns to what the user saved.

The value is written to the value of the same name under HKCU\Software\Policies\KashiharaCity\ksip. KSIP reads it when it starts, so a change takes effect when KSIP starts again.</string>
      <string id="rtp_port">First RTP port</string>
      <string id="rtp_port_Help">The first port for audio (RTP): an even number from 1024 to 65400; 20 ports from it are used. An odd number, or an overlap with the SIP port, is refused at connect. Disabled deletes the value and, as not configured, returns to the user's own. (default: 10000)

A setting a policy decides cannot be changed in the KSIP settings dialog or the button editing, and is shown as set by the administrator. Not configured returns to what the user saved.

The value is written to the value of the same name under HKCU\Software\Policies\KashiharaCity\ksip. KSIP reads it when it starts, so a change takes effect when KSIP starts again.</string>
      <string id="pbx_only">Take calls from the registrar PBX only</string>
      <string id="pbx_only_Help">Whether calls and requests from anywhere but the PBX this phone registers with are refused. When enabled, nothing is taken before registering, and over TCP and TLS nothing is listened for (calls come over the registration's connection). Disable it where the PBX sends from more than one address. (default: refused)

A setting a policy decides cannot be changed in the KSIP settings dialog or the button editing, and is shown as set by the administrator. Not configured returns to what the user saved.

The value is written to the value of the same name under HKCU\Software\Policies\KashiharaCity\ksip. KSIP reads it when it starts, so a change takes effect when KSIP starts again.</string>
      <string id="register_interval">Registration interval</string>
      <string id="register_interval_Help">How often (seconds) the registration (REGISTER) is renewed, 30 to 3600. Disabled deletes the value and, as not configured, returns to the user's own. (default: 300)

A setting a policy decides cannot be changed in the KSIP settings dialog or the button editing, and is shown as set by the administrator. Not configured returns to what the user saved.

The value is written to the value of the same name under HKCU\Software\Policies\KashiharaCity\ksip. KSIP reads it when it starts, so a change takes effect when KSIP starts again.</string>
      <string id="aec">Echo cancellation</string>
      <string id="aec_Help">Whether the WebRTC echo canceller (AEC3) is used. Enabled uses it; disabled does not. (default: used)

A setting a policy decides cannot be changed in the KSIP settings dialog or the button editing, and is shown as set by the administrator. Not configured returns to what the user saved.

The value is written to the value of the same name under HKCU\Software\Policies\KashiharaCity\ksip. KSIP reads it when it starts, so a change takes effect when KSIP starts again.</string>
      <string id="high_pass">High-pass filter</string>
      <string id="high_pass_Help">Whether the high-pass filter cuts the low end. (default: used)

A setting a policy decides cannot be changed in the KSIP settings dialog or the button editing, and is shown as set by the administrator. Not configured returns to what the user saved.

The value is written to the value of the same name under HKCU\Software\Policies\KashiharaCity\ksip. KSIP reads it when it starts, so a change takes effect when KSIP starts again.</string>
      <string id="noise_suppression">Noise suppression</string>
      <string id="noise_suppression_Help">How strongly noise is suppressed. Disabled deletes the value and, as not configured, returns to the user's own. (default: high)

A setting a policy decides cannot be changed in the KSIP settings dialog or the button editing, and is shown as set by the administrator. Not configured returns to what the user saved.

The value is written to the value of the same name under HKCU\Software\Policies\KashiharaCity\ksip. KSIP reads it when it starts, so a change takes effect when KSIP starts again.</string>
      <string id="noise_suppression_0">Off</string>
      <string id="noise_suppression_1">Low</string>
      <string id="noise_suppression_2">Moderate</string>
      <string id="noise_suppression_3">High</string>
      <string id="noise_suppression_4">Very high</string>
      <string id="agc">Automatic gain control</string>
      <string id="agc_Help">Whether the WebRTC AGC2 digital gain evens out the voice level. The microphone volume itself is not changed. It lifts a quiet room's noise too, so it is off by default. (default: not used)

A setting a policy decides cannot be changed in the KSIP settings dialog or the button editing, and is shown as set by the administrator. Not configured returns to what the user saved.

The value is written to the value of the same name under HKCU\Software\Policies\KashiharaCity\ksip. KSIP reads it when it starts, so a change takes effect when KSIP starts again.</string>
      <string id="auto_record">Automatic recording</string>
      <string id="auto_record_Help">Whether every call is recorded when it starts. Recordings are kept as MP3 in the user's %LocalAppData%\KashiharaCity\ksip\recordings. (default: not recorded)

A setting a policy decides cannot be changed in the KSIP settings dialog or the button editing, and is shown as set by the administrator. Not configured returns to what the user saved.

The value is written to the value of the same name under HKCU\Software\Policies\KashiharaCity\ksip. KSIP reads it when it starts, so a change takes effect when KSIP starts again.</string>
      <string id="auto_answer">Automatic answer</string>
      <string id="auto_answer_Help">Whether incoming calls are answered at once. Meant for testing. (default: not answered)

A setting a policy decides cannot be changed in the KSIP settings dialog or the button editing, and is shown as set by the administrator. Not configured returns to what the user saved.

The value is written to the value of the same name under HKCU\Software\Policies\KashiharaCity\ksip. KSIP reads it when it starts, so a change takes effect when KSIP starts again.</string>
      <string id="incoming_action">Incoming call while in the tray</string>
      <string id="incoming_action_Help">Whether an incoming call while the window is in the tray shows the window or notifies on the taskbar. Disabled deletes the value and, as not configured, returns to the user's own. (default: show the window)

A setting a policy decides cannot be changed in the KSIP settings dialog or the button editing, and is shown as set by the administrator. Not configured returns to what the user saved.

The value is written to the value of the same name under HKCU\Software\Policies\KashiharaCity\ksip. KSIP reads it when it starts, so a change takes effect when KSIP starts again.</string>
      <string id="incoming_action_0">Show the window</string>
      <string id="incoming_action_1">Notify on the taskbar</string>
      <string id="tray_after_call">Go to the tray after a call</string>
      <string id="tray_after_call_Help">Seconds after the last call ends before the window goes to the tray, 0 to 3600; a call in the meantime calls it off. Disabled deletes the value, and the window stays (the default).

A setting a policy decides cannot be changed in the KSIP settings dialog or the button editing, and is shown as set by the administrator. Not configured returns to what the user saved.

The value is written to the value of the same name under HKCU\Software\Policies\KashiharaCity\ksip. KSIP reads it when it starts, so a change takes effect when KSIP starts again.</string>
      <string id="program_integration">Accept operation from other programs</string>
      <string id="program_integration_Help">Whether other programs may place, answer and end calls, as with ksip.exe ksip:&lt;number&gt;. When not, such a request is refused with exit code 4. Browser ksip: links too work only while this is enabled. (default: not accepted)

A setting a policy decides cannot be changed in the KSIP settings dialog or the button editing, and is shown as set by the administrator. Not configured returns to what the user saved.

The value is written to the value of the same name under HKCU\Software\Policies\KashiharaCity\ksip. KSIP reads it when it starts, so a change takes effect when KSIP starts again.</string>
      <string id="browser_integration">Accept ksip: links</string>
      <string id="browser_integration_Help">Whether ksip: links from the browser (dial, answer, hang up) are accepted. It takes effect only while &quot;Accept operation from other programs&quot; is enabled too; then HKCU\Software\Classes\ksip is registered at start, and otherwise removed. (default: not accepted)

A setting a policy decides cannot be changed in the KSIP settings dialog or the button editing, and is shown as set by the administrator. Not configured returns to what the user saved.

The value is written to the value of the same name under HKCU\Software\Policies\KashiharaCity\ksip. KSIP reads it when it starts, so a change takes effect when KSIP starts again.</string>
      <string id="browser_dial_confirm">Confirm dialling from a link</string>
      <string id="browser_dial_confirm_Help">Whether dialling from a ksip: link asks first. (default: asks)

A setting a policy decides cannot be changed in the KSIP settings dialog or the button editing, and is shown as set by the administrator. Not configured returns to what the user saved.

The value is written to the value of the same name under HKCU\Software\Policies\KashiharaCity\ksip. KSIP reads it when it starts, so a change takes effect when KSIP starts again.</string>
      <string id="language">Display language</string>
      <string id="language_Help">The language of the window. Following Windows falls back to Japanese for a language KSIP has no words for. Disabled deletes the value and, as not configured, returns to the user's own. (default: follow Windows)

A setting a policy decides cannot be changed in the KSIP settings dialog or the button editing, and is shown as set by the administrator. Not configured returns to what the user saved.

The value is written to the value of the same name under HKCU\Software\Policies\KashiharaCity\ksip. KSIP reads it when it starts, so a change takes effect when KSIP starts again.</string>
      <string id="language_0">Follow the Windows display language</string>
      <string id="language_1">Japanese</string>
      <string id="language_2">English</string>
      <string id="language_3">Traditional Chinese</string>
      <string id="shortcut_window">Key to show or hide the window</string>
      <string id="shortcut_window_Help">The global shortcut that shows or hides the window: modifiers and a key joined by +, such as SHIFT+F2. Disabled deletes the value and, as not configured, returns to the user's own. (default: none)

A setting a policy decides cannot be changed in the KSIP settings dialog or the button editing, and is shown as set by the administrator. Not configured returns to what the user saved.

The value is written to the value of the same name under HKCU\Software\Policies\KashiharaCity\ksip. KSIP reads it when it starts, so a change takes effect when KSIP starts again.</string>
      <string id="shortcut_call">Key to answer or hang up</string>
      <string id="shortcut_call_Help">The global shortcut that answers or hangs up, written as for the window key. Disabled deletes the value and, as not configured, returns to the user's own. (default: none)

A setting a policy decides cannot be changed in the KSIP settings dialog or the button editing, and is shown as set by the administrator. Not configured returns to what the user saved.

The value is written to the value of the same name under HKCU\Software\Policies\KashiharaCity\ksip. KSIP reads it when it starts, so a change takes effect when KSIP starts again.</string>
      <string id="sound_ring">Ring WAV</string>
      <string id="sound_ring_Help">Path of the WAV file played as the ring sound, up to 400 characters. One that cannot be read leaves the built-in sound. Disabled deletes the value and, as not configured, returns to the user's own. (default: built-in)

A setting a policy decides cannot be changed in the KSIP settings dialog or the button editing, and is shown as set by the administrator. Not configured returns to what the user saved.

The value is written to the value of the same name under HKCU\Software\Policies\KashiharaCity\ksip. KSIP reads it when it starts, so a change takes effect when KSIP starts again.</string>
      <string id="sound_ringback">Ringback WAV</string>
      <string id="sound_ringback_Help">Path of the WAV file played as the ringback sound, up to 400 characters. It goes through the call's playback path, so only a 48 kHz mono WAV is taken. One that cannot be read leaves the built-in sound. Disabled deletes the value and, as not configured, returns to the user's own. (default: built-in)

A setting a policy decides cannot be changed in the KSIP settings dialog or the button editing, and is shown as set by the administrator. Not configured returns to what the user saved.

The value is written to the value of the same name under HKCU\Software\Policies\KashiharaCity\ksip. KSIP reads it when it starts, so a change takes effect when KSIP starts again.</string>
      <string id="sound_busy">Busy WAV</string>
      <string id="sound_busy_Help">Path of the WAV file played as the busy sound, up to 400 characters. One that cannot be read leaves the built-in sound. Disabled deletes the value and, as not configured, returns to the user's own. (default: built-in)

A setting a policy decides cannot be changed in the KSIP settings dialog or the button editing, and is shown as set by the administrator. Not configured returns to what the user saved.

The value is written to the value of the same name under HKCU\Software\Policies\KashiharaCity\ksip. KSIP reads it when it starts, so a change takes effect when KSIP starts again.</string>
      <string id="sound_notfound">Number not found WAV</string>
      <string id="sound_notfound_Help">Path of the WAV file played as the number not found sound, up to 400 characters. One that cannot be read leaves the built-in sound. Disabled deletes the value and, as not configured, returns to the user's own. (default: built-in)

A setting a policy decides cannot be changed in the KSIP settings dialog or the button editing, and is shown as set by the administrator. Not configured returns to what the user saved.

The value is written to the value of the same name under HKCU\Software\Policies\KashiharaCity\ksip. KSIP reads it when it starts, so a change takes effect when KSIP starts again.</string>
      <string id="sound_error">Error WAV</string>
      <string id="sound_error_Help">Path of the WAV file played as the error sound, up to 400 characters. One that cannot be read leaves the built-in sound. Disabled deletes the value and, as not configured, returns to the user's own. (default: built-in)

A setting a policy decides cannot be changed in the KSIP settings dialog or the button editing, and is shown as set by the administrator. Not configured returns to what the user saved.

The value is written to the value of the same name under HKCU\Software\Policies\KashiharaCity\ksip. KSIP reads it when it starts, so a change takes effect when KSIP starts again.</string>
      <string id="detail_log">Detailed log</string>
      <string id="detail_log_Help">Whether the log carries detail for troubleshooting: whole SIP messages (authentication headers hidden), baresip debug lines and WebRTC audio processing lines. (default: off)

A setting a policy decides cannot be changed in the KSIP settings dialog or the button editing, and is shown as set by the administrator. Not configured returns to what the user saved.

The value is written to the value of the same name under HKCU\Software\Policies\KashiharaCity\ksip. KSIP reads it when it starts, so a change takes effect when KSIP starts again.</string>
      <string id="button_1">Button 01</string>
      <string id="button_1_Help">Custom button 1. Enabled writes its five values (title, function, number, transfer target, number while in use); disabled deletes all five and no button is shown.

Title: up to 40 characters; empty shows the number (do not disturb and voicemail show their names in the display language).
Function: transfer, dial with BLF, dial without BLF, park with BLF, open a link, do not disturb, voicemail.
Number: digits, * and # (a leading + too), up to 30, or a SIP URI starting with sip:. Dial without BLF also takes the separators - . ( ) and spaces, and tel:. Open a link takes an http:// or https:// URL. Do not disturb takes none.
Transfer target: for park, where the call in progress goes while the number is free; empty means the number.
Number while in use: for dial and park, what is called while the number is in use (a pickup code, say); empty means the number.

Two buttons cannot watch the same number. KSIP does not connect with a value that is not valid. Buttons 1 to 6 sit under the phone; 7 to 30 in expansion unit 1 beside it, 31 to 54 in expansion unit 2 beyond.

A setting a policy decides cannot be changed in the KSIP settings dialog or the button editing, and is shown as set by the administrator. Not configured returns to what the user saved.

The value is written to the value of the same name under HKCU\Software\Policies\KashiharaCity\ksip. KSIP reads it when it starts, so a change takes effect when KSIP starts again.</string>
      <string id="button_2">Button 02</string>
      <string id="button_2_Help">Custom button 2. Enabled writes its five values (title, function, number, transfer target, number while in use); disabled deletes all five and no button is shown.

Title: up to 40 characters; empty shows the number (do not disturb and voicemail show their names in the display language).
Function: transfer, dial with BLF, dial without BLF, park with BLF, open a link, do not disturb, voicemail.
Number: digits, * and # (a leading + too), up to 30, or a SIP URI starting with sip:. Dial without BLF also takes the separators - . ( ) and spaces, and tel:. Open a link takes an http:// or https:// URL. Do not disturb takes none.
Transfer target: for park, where the call in progress goes while the number is free; empty means the number.
Number while in use: for dial and park, what is called while the number is in use (a pickup code, say); empty means the number.

Two buttons cannot watch the same number. KSIP does not connect with a value that is not valid. Buttons 1 to 6 sit under the phone; 7 to 30 in expansion unit 1 beside it, 31 to 54 in expansion unit 2 beyond.

A setting a policy decides cannot be changed in the KSIP settings dialog or the button editing, and is shown as set by the administrator. Not configured returns to what the user saved.

The value is written to the value of the same name under HKCU\Software\Policies\KashiharaCity\ksip. KSIP reads it when it starts, so a change takes effect when KSIP starts again.</string>
      <string id="button_3">Button 03</string>
      <string id="button_3_Help">Custom button 3. Enabled writes its five values (title, function, number, transfer target, number while in use); disabled deletes all five and no button is shown.

