      <string id="button_5">Button 05</string>
      <string id="button_5_Help">Custom button 5. Enabled writes its five values (title, function, number, transfer target, number while in use); disabled deletes all five and no button is shown.

Title: up to 40 characters; empty shows the number (do not disturb and voicemail show their names in the display language).
Function: transfer, dial with BLF, dial without BLF, park with BLF, open a link, do not disturb, voicemail.
Number: digits, * and # (a leading + too), up to 30, or a SIP URI starting with sip:. Dial without BLF also takes the separators - . ( ) and spaces, and tel:. Open a link takes an http:// or https:// URL. Do not disturb takes none.
Transfer target: for park, where the call in progress goes while the number is free; empty means the number.
Number while in use: for dial and park, what is called while the number is in use (a pickup code, say); empty means the number.

Two buttons cannot watch the same number. KSIP does not connect with a value that is not valid. Buttons 1 to 6 sit under the phone; 7 to 30 in expansion unit 1 beside it, 31 to 54 in expansion unit 2 beyond.

A setting a policy decides cannot be changed in the KSIP settings dialog or the button editing, and is shown as set by the administrator. Not configured returns to what the user saved.

The value is written to the value of the same name under HKCU\Software\Policies\KashiharaCity\ksip. KSIP reads it when it starts, so a change takes effect when KSIP starts again.</string>
